Commit:     Magnus Melin <mkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi>
CommitDate: Fri Apr 11 23:15:04 2025 +0000

    Bug 1953100 - Remove nsIMsgWindow.StopUrls() stopped and unused variables. r=heather

    Stop is primarily used from the "Stop" button that can be added to the toolbar, and in relation to a few other operations: search, filtering, and also affecting offline sync on demand.

    This patch removes stopurls and related code.
    I did not come up with a good replacement for stop running filters on demand, so I suggest removing that functionality.
    The related filtering code is not great, so there's no good place to hang the stopper on. We *could* think of something, but
    it does seem like a rather obscure use case especially as filters are usually running quickly.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D241003

